---
/**
 * website/src/pages/keys.astro — where a licence key comes from (portal plan, Task P9.3; the
 * design `docs/key-signing-service/spec.md`).
 *
 * **The page points at the portal and asks nothing.** A licence key — the free evaluation seat,
 * the open-source year, a paid seat — is issued by the signed-in portal, Fugaro's own web app on
 * `app.` plus this site's canonical host (`src/lib/portal.mjs`, the derivation the licence
 * service's own invites use for the same pair, `ee/keyservice/invites.go`). So this page's whole
 * job is to send a reader there: it carries no form and no field, and it collects nothing. Where
 * a reader once filled a form here — the free seat, the open-source programme and the requests a
 * person read, each a POST to the intake — those questions are now the portal's, asked under an
 * account of the reader's own, so the site no longer sends an applicant's data anywhere.
 *
 * **The route and the statement stay.** `/privacy/` links this page (the statement's key sign-up
 * card sends a reader here), so the build keeps `/keys/` and the page keeps its pointer back at
 * the statement. What the service keeps, and for how long, is counsel's and the owner's copy on
 * `/privacy/`, so this page carries the pointer and no sentence of its own about the data;
 * `website/test/privacy.mjs` rule 9 holds the statement's card to this page, and
 * `website/test/consent.mjs` holds the page to the statement's "no form" claim (which is now
 * true of every page, this one included).
 *
 * **The CSP no longer widens for it.** The deployed policy's `form-action` is `'self'` alone
 * again: a form used to post to the intake on `keys.`, the one host the policy admitted beyond
 * `'self'` (S3.3), and with the forms gone the widening is gone with them. The portal is a host
 * the site LINKS to, on `allowed_hosts`, so it is admitted in no directive at all —
 * `website/test/origins.mjs` holds the policy to both halves.
 *
 * The look is the site's (P1's `base.css` §2c): the headline is the display scale's largest step
 * with the accent's gradient on it, and the one card is the site's own `.card`.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { loadSite } from '../content.ts'
import { portalOrigin } from '../lib/portal.mjs'

const facts = loadSite().facts
const portal = portalOrigin(facts.canonicalURL)
---

<Base
  title="Get a key"
  description="Fugaro licence keys come from the portal, Fugaro's own service: sign in and ask for one there."
>
  <div class="keys-head">
    <h1 class="keys-title display-xl"><span class="gradient-text">Get a key</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Fugaro's licence keys come from the portal — Fugaro's own service — where you sign in and
      ask for one. This page asks you for nothing: every question a key needs, you answer there.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="keys-section">
    <p class="keys-note">
      The free evaluation seat, the open-source programme and every request a person reads are
      handled in the portal, under an account of your own. Sign in there and choose the one that
      fits.
    </p>
    <a class="keys-portal" href={portal} rel="noopener">Go to the portal</a>
  </section>

  <p class="keys-privacy">
    What the service keeps, and for how long, is in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy
    statement</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The page's own layout, in the site's tokens (W1.2, D104): no colour is named here, and the
     shapes the site repeats — the display scale, `.gradient-text`, `.card` and the `lede` the
     FAQ opens with — are `base.css` §2c. What is this file's own is the room between its bands,
     the one column the page is laid in, and the portal link, which wears the accent the way a
     page's one action does. */

  .keys-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-xl);
  }

  .keys-title {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .keys-section {
    margin-block: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .keys-note {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* The portal link: the accent as the fill and the ground as the label, the pair `a11y.mjs`
     computes, at the 44 px target the brief of 2026-10-19 measures every control against — the
     one place this page sends a reader, so it wears the accent a button would. */
  .keys-portal {
    display: inline-block;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--ground);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-black);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .keys-privacy {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }
</style>
